{
  "$comment": [
    "Declared probe values for the attribute coverage matrix.",
    "",
    "The matrix flips one attribute at a time away from its default and asserts the",
    "PHP serializer still reproduces the block's real save(). Most values are derived",
    "from the attribute's declared type by Attribute_Probe_Generator. This file covers",
    "the ones that cannot be guessed: objects, arrays, and strings whose valid values",
    "are a convention rather than a declared enum.",
    "",
    "Two sections, most specific first:",
    "  byBlock  '<block name>' -> '<attribute>' -> entry. Always wins.",
    "  byName   '<attribute>' -> entry. Applies to every block declaring that name.",
    "",
    "An entry is { \"probe\": <one value> }, { \"probes\": [ <alternatives> ] }, or",
    "{ \"skip\": \"<reason>\" }. `probe` is ONE value whatever its type, so an array",
    "attribute uses `probe` with an array; `probes` is a list of ALTERNATIVE values,",
    "each producing its own payload. Do not use `probes` for an array-valued",
    "attribute - that sets the attribute to each element in turn.",
    "A skip must say WHY; 'no save() effect' with no explanation is not a reason.",
    "",
    "byName is for genuinely universal conventions only. An attribute whose valid",
    "values differ per block MUST be declared byBlock, never byName - iconPosition is",
    "'right'/'left' on accordion, 'start'/'end' on icon-button and 'top' on counter,",
    "so a single shared probe would be wrong for two of the three.",
    "",
    "Both sections are key-diffed against the live block registry in BOTH directions",
    "by abilities-attribute-probe-table-test.php: an attribute with no probe fails,",
    "and an entry naming an attribute that no longer exists fails too. That is what",
    "stops this file rotting into a list of things that used to be true."
  ],
